('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Place value', 'What is the value of the digit 4 in 5,407?', '4', '40', '400', '4,000', 'C', 'The 4 is in the hundreds place, so its value is 400.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Factors and multiples', 'What is the highest common factor of 18 and 24?', '3', '6', '9', '12', 'B', 'The common factors are 1, 2, 3 and 6; the greatest is 6.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Fractions', 'What is three quarters plus one eighth?', '4/12', '5/8', '7/8', '1', 'C', 'Three quarters is six eighths; six eighths plus one eighth is seven eighths.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Ratio', 'The ratio of red to blue beads is 2:3. If there are 25 beads altogether, how many are red?', '10', '12', '15', '20', 'A', 'There are five equal parts; each part is 5 beads, so red beads number 2 × 5 = 10.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Perimeter', 'A rectangular classroom board is 8 m long and 5 m wide. What is its perimeter?', '13 m', '26 m', '40 m', '80 m', 'B', 'Perimeter = 2 × (length + width) = 2 × (8 + 5) = 26 m.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Angles', 'Two angles lie on a straight line. If one is 65°, what is the other?', '25°', '65°', '115°', '125°', 'C', 'Angles on a straight line sum to 180°, so 180° − 65° = 115°.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Decimals', 'What is 0.6 multiplied by 10?', '0.06', '0.6', '6', '60', 'C', 'Multiplying a decimal by 10 moves the decimal point one place to the right.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Mathematics', 'Statistics', 'Find the mode of 2, 3, 3, 4 and 5.', '2', '3', '4', '5', 'B', 'The mode is the value occurring most often; 3 occurs twice.', 'easy', 1),

('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Parts of speech', 'In “The tall boy carried the bag,” which word is an adjective?', 'The', 'tall', 'carried', 'bag', 'B', 'Tall describes the noun boy, so it is an adjective.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Verbs and tense', 'Choose the sentence that correctly tells what happened yesterday.', 'She writes a letter yesterday.', 'She wrote a letter yesterday.', 'She will write a letter yesterday.', 'She writing a letter yesterday.', 'B', 'Wrote is the past tense of write and agrees with the time marker yesterday.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Vocabulary', 'Which word is closest in meaning to “rapid”?', 'Slow', 'Quick', 'Weak', 'Quiet', 'B', 'Rapid means happening or moving quickly.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Punctuation', 'Which punctuation mark belongs at the end of “Where is my exercise book”?', 'Full stop (.)', 'Comma (,)', 'Question mark (?)', 'Apostrophe (’)', 'C', 'The sentence asks a direct question and ends with a question mark.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Nouns and number', 'What is the correct plural form of “child”?', 'Childs', 'Childes', 'Children', 'Childrens', 'C', 'Children is the standard irregular plural of child.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Sentence structure', 'What is the subject of “The birds flew over the roof”?', 'Flew', 'Over the roof', 'The birds', 'The roof', 'C', 'The birds are the people or things the sentence says something about.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Articles', 'Choose the correct phrase.', 'A honest pupil', 'An honest pupil', 'The honest pupil are', 'Honest an pupil', 'B', 'Honest begins with a vowel sound, so an is used before it.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'English Studies', 'Collective nouns', 'A group of cattle is called a ____.', 'flock', 'herd', 'swarm', 'bouquet', 'B', 'A herd is a group of cattle or other large grazing animals.', 'easy', 1),

('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Human body', 'Which organ helps a person breathe by taking oxygen into the body?', 'Kidneys', 'Lungs', 'Stomach', 'Skin', 'B', 'The lungs exchange oxygen and carbon dioxide during breathing.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'States of matter', 'What is the change from liquid water to water vapour called?', 'Freezing', 'Melting', 'Evaporation', 'Condensation', 'C', 'Evaporation changes a liquid into a gas at its surface.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Plant structure', 'Which plant part mainly absorbs water and mineral salts from the soil?', 'Flower', 'Leaf', 'Root', 'Fruit', 'C', 'Roots take in water and dissolved mineral salts from the soil.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Force and motion', 'Which action shows that a force can change the motion of an object?', 'A book remains on a desk.', 'A resting ball is kicked and rolls.', 'A stone is grey.', 'Water fills a cup.', 'B', 'The kick applies a force that sets the resting ball in motion.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Particles and matter', 'Which statement best describes particles in a solid?', 'They are very far apart and move freely.', 'They are close together and vibrate about fixed positions.', 'They do not exist.', 'They move only when the solid melts.', 'B', 'Solid particles are closely packed and mainly vibrate in fixed positions.', 'medium', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Living things and environment', 'In a simple food chain, which organism is usually a producer?', 'Green plant', 'Goat', 'Hawk', 'Mushroom', 'A', 'Green plants make food using sunlight and form the base of many food chains.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Laboratory safety', 'What should a learner do if an unknown chemical spills on the laboratory bench?', 'Taste it to identify it.', 'Touch it with bare hands.', 'Tell the teacher and follow safety instructions.', 'Mix it with another chemical.', 'C', 'A learner should alert the teacher and follow the correct spill procedure.', 'easy', 1),
('JSS1', null, 'Intermediate Science', 'Energy and plants', 'Which source of energy is needed by green plants to make food?', 'Moonlight', 'Sunlight', 'Sound', 'Wind alone', 'B', 'Plants use light energy in photosynthesis.', 'easy', 1),

('JSS1', null, 'Digital Technologies', 'Computer components', 'Which computer component carries out instructions and processes data?', 'Monitor', 'Central processing unit', 'Keyboard', 'Loudspeaker', 'B', 'The central processing unit (CPU) processes instructions and data.', 'easy', 1),
